DREAM macOS port: faad2 2.11.4 DRM fix 2/2 - decode MPEG-4 PS in DRM mode.

ETSI ES 201 980 V4.x clause 5.4.3: 'The MPEG PS tool as specified in MPEG-4 Audio
is used'; table 14: bs_extension_id 2 = MPEG PARAMETRIC STEREO, 0 'shall not be
used'. faad2 parsed MPEG PS data in DRM mode but then always ran the legacy DRM
PS synthesis (drm_ps_decode, id 0), which without DRM PS data just copies L to
R: PS streams came out mono without an error. Now the MPEG PS synthesis is used
whenever MPEG PS data was received; legacy DRM PS streams behave as before.

diff --git a/libfaad/sbr_dec.c b/libfaad/sbr_dec.c
index 13e66ff..0c07c7d 100644
--- a/libfaad/sbr_dec.c
+++ b/libfaad/sbr_dec.c
@@ -661,9 +661,13 @@ uint8_t sbrDecodeSingleFramePS(sbr_info *sbr, real_t *left_channel, real_t *righ
     }
 
     /* perform parametric stereo */
+    /* DRM: ETSI ES 201 980 V3+ uses MPEG-4 PS (bs_extension_id 2, "id 0 shall
+       not be used"); the legacy DRM PS (id 0) is only used when it is the PS
+       data actually received (DREAM macOS port patch). */
 #ifdef DRM_PS
-    if (sbr->Is_DRM_SBR)
+    if (sbr->Is_DRM_SBR && sbr->ps == NULL)
     {
+        /* legacy DRM PS, or no PS data yet (drm_ps_decode copies L to R) */
         drm_ps_decode(sbr->drm_ps, (sbr->ret > 0), X_left, X_right);
     } else {
 #endif
